Q: How to remove reverse extra line? A: <p>The reverse of <code>"1234567\n"</code> is <code>"\n7654321"</code>. If you want to strip out the newline before reversing, you can use <a href="http://perldoc.perl.org/functions/chomp.html" rel="noreferrer">the built-in <code>chomp</code> function</a>:</p>

<pre><code>while(&lt;STDIN&gt;){
  chomp;
  my $reverse = reverse $_; #(explicit - to force casting)
  if( 5 &lt;length ){
        print "Reverse is $reverse\n";
  }
  else{
    print "$_\n"; #this will print $_ scalar context
  }
}
</code></pre>
